From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 10:32:28 +0000
Subject: mkw-no-lag-kart: Mario Kart World fixes from kingbumi31/no-lag-kart

Ported from kingbumi31/no-lag-kart (MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 seedds; the fork's own commits by
Bumi), a Mario Kart World 1.8.0 fork of nxnative tuned on a 16 GB M2 Pro. Only what nxnative's
main at the pin does not already have, in another form or this one:

- A memory pool's Finalize costs what the pool holds (aa3d115b, 9b1f285a): the pool address
  index is put right by an insertion sort instead of sorted anew; the texture IDs are listed by
  pool, so a Finalize marks its own IDs gone instead of walking all 131,000; the view cache is
  walked only for a pool that has sets in it. Their runs: the 50-70 ms freeze once per stretch
  of track went from 14 of 17 runs to 1 of 12.
- A sparse texture shares storage only with pools its pool has mapped pages of
  (nvn_sparse_shares, d67d32a3): the sky's cube map no longer splits its passes, 6 -> 1 a view.
- Upload sources copied into a resident ring (DM_NVN_UP_COPY, profile key up_copy, 1ec15ff8)
  instead of a zero-copy buffer made resident per upload: a scene cut's residency work halves,
  its frame 20-28 ms shorter. Rewritten for up_big_src's staging budget.
- Mario Kart World's profile: enc_thread on, nvn_cut 8 (new profile key; DM_NVN_CUT still
  overrides), up_copy 128.

Already in nxnative (left out): the 1.8.0 frame step and its 2-vsync cap, the written-pages
commit walk, the BAHS control-section row, PRs #2225 #2249 #2328 #2228 #2182, #2091 (0051), and
face-split draws for the cube filters (what pso_whole, fs_split and DM_NVN_FS_LAYER did).
Left out on purpose: the streamed submission (the submit path now also snapshots ray-tracing
structures under the lock), the GPU clock keeper of PR #1847, the host PGO profile, PR #1230
(rebuilds every shader), the merged warm-up list, DM_OPMODE_MULTI and the timestamp pad.

Tests: t_pool_finalize (new, adapted: the view cache is keyed by Metal texture here) and
t_copy_alias's sparse_shares case, both from the fork.

